  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>Lomefloxacin is a fluoroquinolone antibiotic used against bacterial infections such as urinary tract infections, bronchitis, and eye infections including conjunctivitis. It is an approved medicine, available as tablets for systemic use and as eye drops, though it is not authorised in the European Union.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q203618&quot;>Wikidata Q203618</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><table><tr><td>name:</td><td>lomefloxacin</td></tr><tr><td>ATC codes:</td><td>J01MA07, S01AE04</td></tr><tr><td>DrugBank:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://go.drugbank.com/drugs/DB00978&quot;>DB00978</a></td></tr><tr><td>PubChem CID:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/3948&quot;>3948</a></td></tr><tr><td>ChEBI:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.ebi.ac.uk/chebi/searchId.do?chebiId=CHEBI:116278&quot;>116278</a></td></tr><tr><td>Wikidata:</td><td><a href=&quot;https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q203618&quot;>Q203618</a></td></tr><tr><td>formula:</td><td>C17H19F2N3O3</td></tr><tr><td>molar mass:</td><td>351.353 g/mol (PubChem)</td></tr></table></body></html>"));
